WEBVTT

01:04.689 --> 01:05.857
A long time ago,

01:07.567 --> 01:12.197
there lived a beautiful girl in a castle
located deep inside the forest.

01:16.910 --> 01:19.245
She was always alone,
so she was lonely and bored.

01:20.163 --> 01:24.250
So one day, she left the castle
to find herself a friend to play with.

01:27.545 --> 01:30.799
She offered them
all sorts of amazing gifts,

01:31.299 --> 01:33.093
but nobody ever accepted her.

01:34.803 --> 01:37.555
Later on, she found out why.

01:39.057 --> 01:41.392
A monster who brings along
the shadow of death.

01:42.018 --> 01:43.645
That's what the people called her.

01:44.896 --> 01:47.023
"She's a monster. A monster."

01:51.486 --> 01:54.114
She was very angry
at every living soul in the world.

01:54.948 --> 01:57.033
And she needed to take it out on someone.

02:30.692 --> 02:34.696
Ever since she unexpectedly saved
the boy from dying,

02:35.947 --> 02:40.201
the scary shadow that always
followed her around suddenly disappeared.

02:43.580 --> 02:46.875
And the boy always
followed her around instead.

02:48.501 --> 02:51.588
He always went with her
whether it was day or night

02:52.338 --> 02:54.591
and whether she was in the mountains
or a field.

02:57.760 --> 03:00.680
On a clear and sunny day,
the girl asked him this.

03:01.347 --> 03:04.934
"Hey, will you always stay by my side?"

03:05.935 --> 03:08.396
"Of course. I will never run away."

03:10.648 --> 03:11.649
"Even if I do this?"

03:27.832 --> 03:29.417
The girl was all alone again,

03:30.084 --> 03:32.754
and the shadow of death came back
and whispered this.

03:35.757 --> 03:38.134
"No one can ever stay by your side

03:39.677 --> 03:43.139
because you're a monster.

03:44.474 --> 03:48.394
Do not ever forget that.
Do you understand?"

03:49.604 --> 03:51.940
Yes, Mother.

03:59.364 --> 04:02.575
CHAPTER ONE
THE BOY WHO FED ON NIGHTMARES

04:11.542 --> 04:14.712
This stop is Daun Vocational School.

04:15.421 --> 04:17.757
The next stop is...

04:25.682 --> 04:29.435
I mean, he threw a huge fit
in the middle of class.

04:29.519 --> 04:30.687
My goodness.

04:31.145 --> 04:32.438
No!

04:39.070 --> 04:40.947
There's no use in trying to stop him.

04:41.531 --> 04:43.157
And this isn't the first time.

04:43.241 --> 04:44.575
Your expression...

04:44.659 --> 04:46.995
What if there was a dangerous tool
next to him?

04:47.078 --> 04:48.663
It would've led to an accident.

04:58.631 --> 05:01.426
I don't understand
why we need to walk on eggshells

05:01.509 --> 05:03.386
- because of Sang-tae.
- Is he angry?

05:03.469 --> 05:04.721
Is he angry?

05:06.097 --> 05:08.182
Anyway, we need to think of safety,

05:08.266 --> 05:10.310
- and he's too much for us to handle.
- Angry…

05:10.393 --> 05:14.564
Just send him to a special needs school
or a local community center.

05:14.647 --> 05:16.899
That will be best for everyone.

05:16.983 --> 05:20.236
- Your expression shows your emotions
- Tell me what you think.

05:20.528 --> 05:21.612
What do you think?

05:22.196 --> 05:24.657
Will you please say something?
My gosh, seriously.

05:40.798 --> 05:41.883
He's angry.

05:42.300 --> 05:44.052
THE BOY WHO FED ON NIGHTMARES

06:06.366 --> 06:07.575
MOON SANG-TAE

06:25.510 --> 06:26.344
Sang-tae.

06:28.554 --> 06:29.555
Aren't you hungry?

06:35.937 --> 06:37.355
What do you want to eat?

06:41.234 --> 06:43.444
You weren't planning to stay
for long anyway.

06:46.531 --> 06:49.450
I'll find you a better school
once we move. I promise.

06:55.581 --> 06:57.417
- Are you that upset?
- Jjamppong.

06:57.500 --> 06:59.502
- What?
- Tangsuyuk with sauce on the side.

06:59.585 --> 07:02.338
Let's go to Yangjagang, not Jageumseong.

07:04.173 --> 07:06.884
Okay, let's stuff ourselves with food
at Yangjagang.

07:06.968 --> 07:09.303
The food is really good there.
Do you remember?

07:10.930 --> 07:12.807
When was the last time we went?

07:13.224 --> 07:15.309
Don't worry. I'll buy.
I'm your big brother.

08:19.499 --> 08:22.084
By any chance,
are you Author Ko Mun-yeong?

08:23.419 --> 08:25.463
- Yes.
- See? I told you.

08:26.506 --> 08:29.217
My daughter is a big fan of yours.

08:29.550 --> 08:31.052
I'm sorry to ask this,

08:32.929 --> 08:34.805
but can we please get your autograph?

08:42.438 --> 08:44.857
- Your name?
- Lee Seul-bi.

08:45.775 --> 08:48.486
She's really beautiful in real life,
isn't she?

08:48.569 --> 08:52.281
Yes, she's like a princess
from a fairy tale.

09:00.081 --> 09:02.583
- Why do you think so?
- Because you're pretty.

09:03.209 --> 09:06.420
My mom always calls me "princess"

09:06.796 --> 09:07.838
because I'm pretty.

09:12.843 --> 09:14.887
Ma'am, how about a photo?

09:14.971 --> 09:16.556
My goodness, thank you.

09:16.639 --> 09:17.890
Go stand next to her.

09:19.976 --> 09:20.810
Come here.

09:25.898 --> 09:28.609
You're not my fan, are you?

09:30.319 --> 09:31.153
Pardon?

09:31.737 --> 09:35.408
In all my fairy tales,
the witch is always the one that's pretty.

09:37.159 --> 09:40.079
Who told you
all princesses are kind and pretty?

09:40.871 --> 09:42.248
Did your mom tell you that?

09:42.331 --> 09:44.792
Princess, look over here.

09:45.501 --> 09:49.088
If you really want to be that pretty,
I want you to say this.

09:49.171 --> 09:51.465
- One.
- "Mom.

09:52.383 --> 09:54.552
- I'm going to be...
- Two.

09:55.177 --> 09:58.306
a pretty witch."

09:58.889 --> 09:59.724
Three.

10:06.272 --> 10:07.440
Princess.

10:07.523 --> 10:10.443
- Oh, goodness.
- Princess!

10:12.445 --> 10:14.030
My gosh.

10:17.366 --> 10:18.618
My gosh. Mun-yeong.

10:22.622 --> 10:24.248
Buongiorno, Mun-yeong.

10:25.124 --> 10:28.127
My gosh, what's with this chain?

10:30.546 --> 10:33.257
What made that little kid
cry her eyes out?

10:33.341 --> 10:36.218
I guess she was touched.
I corrected her misconception.

10:37.428 --> 10:38.721
What in the world...

10:41.098 --> 10:42.224
Good job.

10:42.725 --> 10:46.354
It can be very dangerous
for a kid to be biased towards something.

10:46.437 --> 10:48.105
But you helped her fix that?

10:48.773 --> 10:51.609
You really are amazing, Mun-yeong.

10:52.902 --> 10:53.736
Just a second.

10:56.364 --> 10:57.239
OK PSYCHIATRIC HOSPITAL

10:57.323 --> 10:59.492
I don't need a loan. I'm already rich.

11:02.953 --> 11:04.789
Okay, let's get going.

11:04.872 --> 11:06.415
We have about two hours.

11:06.499 --> 11:09.710
- So you have time to go to a beauty salon.
- Why would I go there?

11:11.796 --> 11:13.464
You can't go looking like that.

11:15.132 --> 11:17.551
You look like Francesca who's on her way

11:17.635 --> 11:19.720
to a funeral for the Addams Family.

11:19.804 --> 11:22.390
You can't go to a children's ward
looking like that.

11:22.765 --> 11:26.394
You're going there to give kids hope,
not to scare them.

11:26.477 --> 11:28.145
You'll be reading your books there.

11:28.229 --> 11:30.981
- But you look--
- You said it's dangerous to be biased.

11:31.399 --> 11:33.484
I think you're more dangerous.

11:34.610 --> 11:36.946
Mun-yeong, please.

11:37.029 --> 11:39.031
You should dress according to the TPO.

11:45.955 --> 11:48.207
I'll tell them to come to you.

11:50.668 --> 11:52.753
Do you know why I like this restaurant?

11:53.879 --> 11:57.133
- Because the steak--
- No.

11:59.260 --> 12:00.386
The knife here

12:01.679 --> 12:02.555
is amazing.

12:05.516 --> 12:07.518
- Look.
- Mun-yeong, you're bleeding.

12:09.395 --> 12:10.730
How pretty.

12:12.773 --> 12:13.607
I want it.

12:18.028 --> 12:19.655
Good gracious.

12:22.408 --> 12:23.284
Ma'am.

12:25.619 --> 12:26.495
Just a second.

12:58.319 --> 13:00.529
EMPLOYEE CARD CAREGIVER MOON GANG-TAE

13:02.281 --> 13:04.074
Mr. Moon, come to the lounge quick.

13:09.705 --> 13:13.626
Gosh, that thief ate all my food.

13:14.084 --> 13:15.753
It's as if she starved for days.

13:24.970 --> 13:25.930
Ms. Myoung Ji-suk.

13:29.892 --> 13:30.726
Honey.

13:39.193 --> 13:40.861
I feel so empty.

13:41.779 --> 13:44.198
Even so,
if you eat in such a hurry,

13:45.032 --> 13:47.201
you'll get an upset stomach again.

13:47.284 --> 13:49.745
So don't eat everything all at once.

13:51.247 --> 13:53.624
Instead, it'd be great
if you could take your time

13:54.792 --> 13:56.585
to eat your food.

13:57.002 --> 13:58.921
You told me you liked that I ate well.

14:00.589 --> 14:02.633
You took it the wrong way.

14:02.716 --> 14:06.262
It's just that when you like someone,
you even like the way they eat.

14:10.516 --> 14:11.600
Honey.

14:14.728 --> 14:15.729
Then

14:17.439 --> 14:22.236
why did you cheat on me
with that skinny model?

15:16.665 --> 15:17.499
It's okay.

15:19.877 --> 15:21.003
Don't smile at me.

15:22.338 --> 15:23.505
It disgusts me.

15:27.760 --> 15:30.471
- Put your arms up like this.
- Let me go!

15:30.554 --> 15:32.598
Then pull them down like this.

15:32.681 --> 15:34.767
- Stay still!
- I don't belong here!

15:34.850 --> 15:37.519
Let me go! Let go of me!

15:37.603 --> 15:39.563
I can't go in here! I can't!

15:39.980 --> 15:43.067
Let go! I don't belong here!

15:43.150 --> 15:44.610
- Is he a new patient?
- Let go!

15:44.693 --> 15:47.321
He overdosed on alprazolam
with his daughter two days ago

15:47.404 --> 15:48.530
and came through the ER.

15:48.614 --> 15:51.075
He used to get treated
for his anxiety disorder.

15:51.158 --> 15:53.327
I think he tried
to commit suicide with her.

15:53.410 --> 15:56.872
I think he wanted to kill his daughter
and then kill himself.

15:56.956 --> 15:58.040
Where's Go-eun?

15:58.123 --> 16:01.377
Where is Go-eun? Where is my daughter?

16:01.460 --> 16:04.213
Fortunately, she threw up
right after she took the drug.

16:04.296 --> 16:07.967
And she's getting counseling for PTSD
at our child psychology department.

16:08.759 --> 16:09.593
Go-eun.

16:10.678 --> 16:11.887
What's on your mind?

16:13.889 --> 16:15.182
Let me go!

16:15.265 --> 16:17.977
He'll receive
a psychiatric assessment this afternoon.

16:18.060 --> 16:19.645
So check his vitals every hour.

16:19.728 --> 16:22.940
And double-check the restraining band
as you give him an IV fluid.

16:23.524 --> 16:24.358
Okay.

16:25.192 --> 16:27.403
After the reading,
you'll answer questions.

16:27.486 --> 16:30.864
Then you'll give out
your autographed storybooks to the kids.

16:30.948 --> 16:34.576
And you'll be done once you take a photo
with the hospital staff for PR.

16:37.955 --> 16:41.417
I'm not sure if I'm a secretary
or the CEO of a publishing company.

16:42.042 --> 16:44.086
I'm seriously starting to wonder.

16:44.169 --> 16:46.672
I got hired as an art director.

16:46.755 --> 16:50.426
But I had no idea
that I'd be working as your minion.

16:50.634 --> 16:53.137
You told me you'll do anything
during the interview.

16:53.220 --> 16:57.641
Well, I didn't know
you'd make me do physical labor.

16:57.725 --> 17:00.185
I hired you
not knowing that you're not very smart.

17:00.269 --> 17:02.396
What should I do? Should I just fire you?

17:02.980 --> 17:03.814
No.

17:07.026 --> 17:08.485
OK PSYCHIATRIC HOSPITAL

17:10.029 --> 17:11.405
“OK Psychiatric Hospital”?

17:12.489 --> 17:13.991
Sir, do you get counseling?

17:14.408 --> 17:16.285
You did the right thing.

17:18.537 --> 17:19.413
Answer the phone.

17:25.044 --> 17:27.171
- Hello?
- Put it on speaker.

17:30.090 --> 17:32.384
Hello? Mr. Lee?

17:33.719 --> 17:36.388
I'm Nam Ju-ri,
a nurse at OK Psychiatric Hospital.

17:36.764 --> 17:37.973
Come this way.

17:38.348 --> 17:41.727
It's so hard to reach you.
You never text us back either.

17:43.479 --> 17:44.813
Are you listening?

17:45.314 --> 17:48.317
Oh, yes. I'm a bit busy--

17:48.400 --> 17:49.651
I believe we told you

17:50.069 --> 17:52.446
that we set a date
for Mr. Ko Dae-hwan's surgery.

17:55.574 --> 17:57.242
How long do we need to wait

17:58.577 --> 18:00.287
for the guardian's consent?

18:01.080 --> 18:03.624
You can't keep avoiding
our calls like this.

18:04.958 --> 18:07.086
That's the same thing
as killing the patient.

18:07.961 --> 18:09.046
Ko Dae-hwan.

18:10.547 --> 18:12.216
He's dead to me.

18:13.383 --> 18:16.470
Why do you keep trying
to bring him back to life? Are you Jesus?

18:17.262 --> 18:18.555
- Excuse me.
- Ju-ri.

18:18.972 --> 18:22.476
If you're so desperate,
come and get the signature yourself.

18:45.207 --> 18:46.500
What's wrong? What is it?

18:47.000 --> 18:49.837
- What happened?
- She wants me to come and get it.

18:51.255 --> 18:52.506
Is she out of her mind?

18:52.840 --> 18:54.967
If she's not sane, she should come here.

18:55.259 --> 18:56.176
Ms. Park.

18:57.261 --> 18:58.971
Tell me about his medical history.

19:02.516 --> 19:05.686
- The patient in room 203 with dementia.
- Oh, Mr. Ko Dae-hwan?

19:06.270 --> 19:10.232
He needs to get surgery
due to his glioblastoma relapse.

19:10.315 --> 19:11.775
But his guardian doesn't care?

19:12.693 --> 19:15.279
He has been with us
for the longest period of time.

19:15.362 --> 19:18.782
But his guardian
never once visited or called

19:18.866 --> 19:21.034
which means he's being neglected.

19:21.743 --> 19:25.205
So instead of just calling
his ungrateful guardian,

19:25.289 --> 19:29.418
why don't you actually visit her in person
so that we can save the patient?

19:29.751 --> 19:30.752
What?

19:31.545 --> 19:34.006
Is that really necessary?

19:34.423 --> 19:37.384
You're going to do it, right?
I know you're a professional.

19:38.969 --> 19:41.847
If you let me take the rest of the day
and tomorrow off,

19:42.723 --> 19:44.683
- I'll go see her myself.
- Why two days?

19:45.267 --> 19:47.227
Do you have a boyfriend in Seoul?

19:49.021 --> 19:50.147
I guess you do.

19:50.230 --> 19:52.983
Ju-ri, you have a boyfriend?

19:53.901 --> 19:54.735
No.

19:55.152 --> 19:57.571
Well then, I'll be off soon.

20:00.532 --> 20:02.659
I bet she does have a boyfriend.

20:03.410 --> 20:04.369
She's a traitor.

20:31.188 --> 20:35.692
I don't think
your daughter will be able to come here.

20:45.827 --> 20:47.788
No.

20:47.871 --> 20:49.164
What's the matter?

20:50.749 --> 20:52.417
No!

20:55.796 --> 20:57.130
Die.

20:58.257 --> 21:01.426
If she comes...

21:18.610 --> 21:21.196
FAIRY TALE READING
WITH AUTHOR KO MUN-YEONG

21:24.032 --> 21:24.866
Gang-tae.

21:26.118 --> 21:26.952
Yes?

21:27.953 --> 21:30.497
I heard someone puked on you.

21:31.456 --> 21:33.583
- She even slapped me.
- My gosh.

21:33.667 --> 21:36.628
You should make sure
the day doesn't get worse.

21:37.045 --> 21:40.257
Kim Seung-cheol, who's in isolation,
will be sent to the police--

21:40.340 --> 21:42.676
Yes, I heard. I'll take care of him.

21:43.510 --> 21:46.596
We had a team dinner last night,
and we made a bet.

21:47.431 --> 21:48.307
"A bet"?

21:48.390 --> 21:49.891
"Why does Moon Gang-tae

21:49.975 --> 21:53.937
move from hospital to hospital every year
instead of settling down?"

21:54.354 --> 21:55.397
We tried to guess it.

21:56.231 --> 21:57.482
Number one.

21:58.358 --> 22:01.111
You borrowed lots of money
and you're being chased after.

22:01.194 --> 22:04.323
Number two.
You got yourself in big trouble,

22:04.406 --> 22:06.742
and you're working here
to hide your identity.

22:06.825 --> 22:07.659
Number three.

22:07.743 --> 22:13.290
You get kicked out of every hospital
for hitting on the nurses and patients.

22:15.000 --> 22:17.419
- Which one did you bet on?
- I bet on

22:18.879 --> 22:19.963
number three. Women.

22:20.047 --> 22:22.174
So what's the answer?

22:26.636 --> 22:27.471
Number four.

22:34.394 --> 22:35.228
Men.

22:37.606 --> 22:40.150
Gang-tae. My gosh.

22:40.359 --> 22:41.526
The coffee tastes nice.

22:45.322 --> 22:48.825
- "I'm still going to love you.
- I'm still going to love you.

22:48.909 --> 22:51.787
- You're as pitiful as I am.
- You're as pitiful as I am.

22:51.870 --> 22:53.622
- I'm not pitiful.
- I'm not pitiful.

22:53.705 --> 22:55.499
- Yes, you are.
- Yes, you are.

22:55.707 --> 22:59.795
- You're even treating me like an orphan?
- You're even treating me like an orphan?

23:00.128 --> 23:02.214
- Even if you're not,
- Even if you're not,

23:02.297 --> 23:05.675
- you think and act like an orphan."
- you think and act like an orphan.

23:05.759 --> 23:06.718
AUTHOR KO MUN-YEONG

23:06.802 --> 23:09.012
- "You're ruthless, insecure,
- You're ruthless, 

23:09.096 --> 23:10.806
- thoughtless,
- insecure, thoughtless,

23:10.889 --> 23:13.141
- and empty-hearted.
- and empty-hearted.

23:13.600 --> 23:17.521
- But I'm still going to love you.
- But I'm still going to love you.

23:17.604 --> 23:19.856
- Do you know why?
- Do you know why?

23:19.940 --> 23:22.901
- Because I decided to do so."
- Because I decided to do so.

23:23.360 --> 23:24.694
I also decided...

23:24.778 --> 23:27.864
"I'm still going to love you."

23:31.576 --> 23:32.536
Did you eat?

23:32.619 --> 23:34.996
I ate jjamppong. Jjamppong.

23:35.080 --> 23:37.290
Again? You need to stop eating noodles.

23:37.749 --> 23:40.544
I bought you some side dishes yesterday.
What are you doing?

23:40.877 --> 23:42.337
I'm drawing.

23:42.421 --> 23:44.840
You're drawing on that woman's book again.

23:44.923 --> 23:48.051
It's not "that woman."
She's writer Ko Mun-yeong.

23:50.137 --> 23:51.263
Yes, Ko Mun-yeong.

23:52.681 --> 23:54.349
She's coming to our hospital today.

23:56.893 --> 23:59.271
She'll be reading her book
to the children here.

24:02.149 --> 24:03.150
Sang-tae?

24:03.942 --> 24:07.112
I'll go. I'll go there.
I'll go there right now.

24:07.195 --> 24:08.738
I'll take blue bus, number 243,

24:08.822 --> 24:11.074
get off at Jayang intersection,
and take 5413,

24:11.158 --> 24:12.909
- the green bus.
- Sang-tae. No, wait.

24:12.993 --> 24:15.704
Get off at Myungsung University
Medical Center and walk--

24:15.787 --> 24:16.830
Moon Sang-tae!

24:21.585 --> 24:22.794
Take three deep breaths.

24:35.223 --> 24:38.852
Listen to me carefully.
Even if you leave now, you'll be late.

24:38.935 --> 24:41.354
Plus, it's only for the children
at our hospital.

24:41.646 --> 24:43.565
But you're not a child, are you?

24:43.648 --> 24:46.693
Moon Sang-tae. 35 years old.
Born in 1984, the year of the rat.

24:46.776 --> 24:48.778
I'm younger than I look,
but I'm not a child.

24:48.862 --> 24:50.155
Exactly. You're an adult.

24:50.906 --> 24:53.783
But instead,
I'll get you an autograph if I can.

24:55.118 --> 24:58.038
Meeting her is a one-time thing,
but autographs last forever.

24:59.164 --> 25:01.750
- Which one do you think is better?
- Her autograph.

25:05.921 --> 25:07.506
Who do you like more, me or her?

25:16.723 --> 25:19.184
Hello? Sang-tae?

25:27.359 --> 25:29.986
I didn't want to ruin her mood
prior to the big event.

25:30.070 --> 25:31.613
That's why I kept it quiet.

25:32.572 --> 25:35.033
I was going to convince her
and take her there

25:35.116 --> 25:37.786
after she successfully finished
today's reading.

25:37.869 --> 25:39.287
Darn it. I totally messed up.

25:42.123 --> 25:43.208
I have a bad feeling.

25:43.291 --> 25:46.628
Why does Ms. Ko hate her father so much?

25:46.711 --> 25:49.005
She hates everyone apart from herself.

25:49.089 --> 25:51.716
Don't even ask why.
That's just how she was born.

25:52.384 --> 25:54.928
If you want to live a long life,
just stay quiet.

25:56.263 --> 25:59.599
Gosh, where in the world is she?
It's almost time.

26:16.032 --> 26:16.866
Excuse me.

26:26.001 --> 26:28.128
- Can you please--
- This is my last one.

26:28.545 --> 26:30.797
No, I don't want one. Can you put it out?

26:31.381 --> 26:34.384
- I just lit it up.
- You can't smoke here so put it out.

27:20.639 --> 27:23.642
Do you believe in destiny?

27:24.476 --> 27:26.686
- What?
- You heard me.

27:30.982 --> 27:32.442
Who cares about destiny?

27:34.611 --> 27:37.989
If someone shows up when you need them,

27:38.823 --> 27:40.158
you call that destiny.

27:59.803 --> 28:02.389
THE BOY WHO FED ON NIGHTMARES

28:04.099 --> 28:05.809
Gosh, that was so loud.

28:11.272 --> 28:14.025
Very realistic, isn't it?
She's good at acting, too.

28:23.910 --> 28:28.415
"The boy woke up
from another awful nightmare.

28:31.793 --> 28:34.921
Bad memories from the past
that he wanted to forget

28:35.380 --> 28:37.924
were replayed in his dreams every night

28:38.007 --> 28:40.844
and haunted him nonstop.

28:44.431 --> 28:46.266
He was terrified of falling asleep.

28:46.349 --> 28:49.686
So one day,
he went to the witch and begged.

28:51.730 --> 28:55.400
'Please get rid of all my bad memories

28:56.234 --> 28:59.237
so that I won't ever have
a nightmare again.

29:01.531 --> 29:05.577
Then I will do everything you ask.'"

29:08.788 --> 29:09.622
Go-eun!

29:10.498 --> 29:13.376
- Go-eun!
- My goodness, what's wrong with you?

29:14.127 --> 29:15.378
Where is Go-eun?

29:16.546 --> 29:17.464
Go-eun!

29:20.133 --> 29:23.136
Go-eun. Where is Go-eun?

29:24.095 --> 29:26.514
Seagull 777. I repeat. Seagull 777.

29:26.598 --> 29:30.268
A NON-PROVOCATIVE CODE FOR PATIENTS
WHO ESCAPE FROM THEIR WARDS

29:38.526 --> 29:40.653
- Hello.
- And lie on your stomach.

29:43.114 --> 29:44.073
Let's try again.

29:44.157 --> 29:45.325
- Are you serious?
- Sorry.

29:45.408 --> 29:48.203
- He felt trapped so I untied him.
- You have restraint straps?

29:48.286 --> 29:49.370
Oh, I forgot.

29:57.670 --> 30:00.173
Look to your right and hold onto your arm.

30:01.925 --> 30:03.718
Let's try it one more time.

30:06.721 --> 30:09.182
"Years went by,
and the boy became an adult.

30:09.599 --> 30:11.768
- He no longer had nightmares.
- Go-eun.

30:11.851 --> 30:16.064
But for some strange reason,
he wasn't happy at all."

30:16.898 --> 30:18.483
- Go-eun.
- What's your problem?

30:19.442 --> 30:21.110
Go-eun.

30:21.986 --> 30:23.780
Gosh, what are you doing?

30:24.531 --> 30:27.075
"One night,
a blood moon filled the night sky,

30:27.158 --> 30:29.035
and the witch finally showed up again

30:29.118 --> 30:32.455
to take what he had promised
in return for granting his wish.

30:32.539 --> 30:36.292
And he shouted at her
with so much resentment.

30:37.502 --> 30:39.963
'All my bad memories are gone.

30:41.840 --> 30:42.674
But why...

30:43.466 --> 30:46.010
Why can't I become happy?'

30:46.803 --> 30:50.014
Then the witch took his soul
as they had promised,

30:50.473 --> 30:51.933
and told him this."

30:55.103 --> 30:56.855
- What's going on?
- Mom!

30:56.938 --> 30:59.065
What the hell is happening?

31:00.567 --> 31:04.779
We unfortunately have to end this here
due to unforeseen circumstances.

31:04.863 --> 31:07.115
All staff and guardians,
please take all children

31:07.574 --> 31:09.784
- back to the ward immediately.
- Go-eun.

31:09.868 --> 31:13.913
Go-eun.

31:14.789 --> 31:17.041
- This isn't over yet.
- Go-eun.

31:17.208 --> 31:18.626
Kids, it's not over.

31:18.710 --> 31:20.503
- Come on.
- Go on.

31:20.587 --> 31:23.339
- Damn it.
- Gosh.

31:23.423 --> 31:25.008
- Mom!
- Mom, I'm scared.

31:25.091 --> 31:26.092
Okay, let's go.

31:27.802 --> 31:28.678
Hello?

31:29.971 --> 31:30.805
Damn it.

31:31.222 --> 31:32.807
Go up.

31:32.891 --> 31:34.517
- Hey!
- Let's go up.

31:34.767 --> 31:36.644
Wait! Wait up.

31:37.395 --> 31:39.188
Go-eun! My gosh, Go-eun...

31:40.064 --> 31:41.107
Come with Daddy.

31:41.190 --> 31:42.859
- Who are you to end this?
- No!

31:42.942 --> 31:44.944
- Right before the climax.
- Let me--

31:45.028 --> 31:46.988
Is it something like "to be continued"?

31:47.071 --> 31:48.865
- It's all right.
- No, I'm scared.

31:49.699 --> 31:50.825
Bring the kids back.

31:50.909 --> 31:52.118
Come on. Let's go.

31:52.869 --> 31:54.495
There are only a few lines left,

31:55.496 --> 31:57.290
so they can leave when it's done.

31:57.790 --> 31:59.208
- You should evacuate--
- Now!

32:11.179 --> 32:13.681
Dad, don't be like this.

32:14.307 --> 32:15.767
I'm scared.

32:17.602 --> 32:18.478
Listen carefully.

32:18.561 --> 32:21.814
If we get caught, I'll be locked away
in a mental institution,

32:21.898 --> 32:23.733
and you'll end up in an orphanage.

32:24.150 --> 32:26.277
Will you be okay
if you can never see me again?

32:26.361 --> 32:29.072
I want to live. I don't want to die.

32:30.239 --> 32:31.240
I told you.

32:31.324 --> 32:34.118
Kids can never live on their own.

32:34.953 --> 32:36.287
If we must be separated,

32:36.371 --> 32:38.289
it'd be better to die together.

32:40.124 --> 32:41.501
What the...

32:43.586 --> 32:44.921
That's such bullshit.

32:48.091 --> 32:51.177
You're a worthless human being
I haven't seen in a while.

32:52.011 --> 32:53.304
Look at that gross face.

32:53.888 --> 32:55.890
Who are you? Do you have a death wish?

32:56.474 --> 32:58.267
Have you ever killed anyone?

33:00.103 --> 33:02.021
You can't carry on with your life,

33:02.105 --> 33:04.607
yet you can't even muster up the courage
to die alone.

33:05.608 --> 33:08.861
So you're trying to lure this kid
into going down that road first.

33:09.112 --> 33:10.321
What?

33:11.072 --> 33:12.782
Don't be such a loser.

33:12.865 --> 33:14.867
Go ahead and take your life alone.

33:15.451 --> 33:16.786
You crazy bitch!

33:27.797 --> 33:29.215
A knife...

33:33.678 --> 33:34.887
Hey!

33:39.058 --> 33:40.309
You piece of...

33:58.536 --> 34:00.872
- Are you all right?
- My dad is...

34:10.006 --> 34:11.758
Who are you to meddle in my affairs?

34:12.216 --> 34:13.217
She's my child.

34:13.384 --> 34:16.512
I can kill her if I want to.
I can do whatever I want with her!

34:17.096 --> 34:20.058
Choke me. Choke me harder, you moron.

34:20.141 --> 34:21.392
You lunatic!

34:21.934 --> 34:24.771
Die. Just die!

34:33.613 --> 34:34.572
It'll be quick.

34:35.990 --> 34:38.117
It'll just be a moment.

34:38.201 --> 34:40.453
It'll end even before you know it.

34:45.291 --> 34:48.044
Die. Just die.

34:48.544 --> 34:50.546
- Die!
- Mr. Kim Seung-cheol!

34:54.634 --> 34:56.594
Let go. Get off me!

34:57.595 --> 34:58.971
You piece of...

34:59.889 --> 35:00.890
Come here.

35:15.029 --> 35:16.531
Let go. Let go of me!

35:18.825 --> 35:21.369
Let go, you bastard! I'll kill you all!

35:21.577 --> 35:24.122
- Let go!
- I'm doing this so that you won't be hurt,

35:24.205 --> 35:25.039
so calm down!

35:25.123 --> 35:27.834
I'll kill you all. I'm going to kill...

36:39.780 --> 36:42.283
THE BOY WHO FED ON NIGHTMARES 

36:44.035 --> 36:47.079
So it wasn't destiny after all.

36:51.292 --> 36:53.419
I'd appreciate it
if you could stay out of this.

36:54.295 --> 36:55.379
Let go of the knife.

36:57.423 --> 36:58.341
He's a patient.

36:59.258 --> 37:00.092
No.

37:01.010 --> 37:02.053
He is not a patient.

37:04.931 --> 37:05.765
He's vermin.

37:08.434 --> 37:11.812
She's crazy. She's completely nuts.

37:12.813 --> 37:13.981
She's insane!

37:22.240 --> 37:25.743
That crazy bitch.
I nearly died because of that bitch!

37:26.577 --> 37:28.996
Let go. Let go of me, you idiots.

37:29.080 --> 37:31.958
Get her, not me.
She's the one who needs help!

37:32.041 --> 37:33.668
- Don't lose him.
- Let go!

37:34.335 --> 37:36.170
Get that insane woman in there!

37:36.462 --> 37:37.713
Let go!

37:47.890 --> 37:50.434
Is the knife hurt?
Why are you wrapping the knife?

37:53.020 --> 37:55.898
If he's non compos mentis,
we can say I acted in self-defense.

37:56.315 --> 38:00.236
I just wanted to give him a small cut,
but you overreacted and hurt yourself.

38:02.405 --> 38:03.239
Here.

38:06.951 --> 38:08.452
Your hand, not the knife.

38:11.622 --> 38:13.249
Here's my special service.

38:14.250 --> 38:15.167
You know what?

38:16.085 --> 38:19.046
In this world,
there are people who deserve to die.

38:20.047 --> 38:22.174
But some thoughtful freaks

38:22.258 --> 38:24.760
kill them for us in secret.

38:25.511 --> 38:28.931
That is why the clueless civilians
can sleep peacefully at night,

38:29.849 --> 38:31.350
completely unaware of it.

38:35.271 --> 38:37.064
Which one do you think I am?

38:50.453 --> 38:51.370
You're

38:53.205 --> 38:54.081
a clueless freak.

39:08.387 --> 39:09.722
Oh, boy.

39:10.473 --> 39:13.642
Thanks to you, my suturing skills
are getting better by the day.

39:15.269 --> 39:17.646
Stop hurting yourself already.

39:22.485 --> 39:23.319
Mr. Moon?

39:24.862 --> 39:25.780
Mr. Moon Gang-tae.

39:27.365 --> 39:28.199
Yes?

39:29.033 --> 39:30.493
What were you thinking about?

39:34.330 --> 39:35.289
It's done.

39:36.040 --> 39:38.667
Okay, fine.
The event turned into total chaos

39:38.751 --> 39:41.962
because of that patient,
so let's just consider it buzz marketing.

39:42.046 --> 39:44.799
But what about the knife fight?
How will you explain it?

39:44.882 --> 39:46.884
One of the hospital staff got hurt.

39:46.967 --> 39:48.969
What if they distribute a press release?

39:49.053 --> 39:51.514
"A famous children's book author
brandished a knife.

39:51.597 --> 39:55.518
Is she working on a martial arts novel?"
You'll see the headlines everywhere.

39:55.601 --> 39:57.561
Just bribe them.
You've done it many times.

39:57.645 --> 40:01.065
- What if that doesn't work?
- We'll use a honey trap. I'll seduce him.

40:09.115 --> 40:09.949
Get in.

40:12.952 --> 40:15.287
You go ahead.
I have to take care of something.

40:15.746 --> 40:17.123
What do you need to do?

40:18.749 --> 40:19.917
Hey, Mun-yeong!

40:20.584 --> 40:22.628
Is she going to cause trouble again?

40:23.170 --> 40:24.004
ADMIN MANAGER

40:24.088 --> 40:26.173
A patient who should've been in isolation

40:26.799 --> 40:28.676
barged in there and ruined the event.

40:29.468 --> 40:33.055
Guardians are calling to complain,
so the phones are ringing off the hook.

40:33.556 --> 40:37.184
We need to quickly find someone
who will take the bullet.

40:39.812 --> 40:42.273
Are you saying I should be that person?

40:42.690 --> 40:45.317
The one who was in charge
of the transfer is new,

40:45.401 --> 40:47.570
so I can't really fire him.

40:48.779 --> 40:50.781
I see here that you've worked

40:51.282 --> 40:54.410
at so many different hospitals
in the past ten years.

40:54.827 --> 40:57.288
My gosh, 15 hospitals in total.

40:58.247 --> 41:01.750
And less than a year at all of them.
You've been here for ten months,

41:02.960 --> 41:05.546
so you'll be quitting soon anyway.

41:05.629 --> 41:06.630
EMPLOYEE CARD

41:09.842 --> 41:11.135
Gang-tae.

41:14.138 --> 41:17.349
I'll say you worked here for a year
and give you the severance pay.

41:18.350 --> 41:19.768
Let's sort it out like that.

41:37.077 --> 41:38.579
Hey, it's me.

41:39.121 --> 41:42.291
Get me the number of the guy
who got hurt because of Mun-yeong.

41:43.417 --> 41:44.793
What do you think?

41:45.044 --> 41:48.339
I need to bribe him to silence him.
Come on. You know the drill.

42:22.873 --> 42:24.708
JAE-SU'S FRIED CHICKEN DELIVERY

42:33.050 --> 42:34.385
I was delivering an order

42:34.468 --> 42:37.555
but saw a guy sitting like a sick chicken
and knew it was you.

42:45.396 --> 42:46.897
Hop on. I'll give you a ride.

42:48.649 --> 42:49.817
You freak.

42:52.736 --> 42:53.654
You're hurt again?

43:13.132 --> 43:14.508
Damn it.

43:15.718 --> 43:17.177
Is he ignoring my calls?

43:18.929 --> 43:22.182
If he bled, I'm sure he'll sue her.

43:23.684 --> 43:25.811
NURSE NAM JU-RI

43:29.982 --> 43:31.233
Hello, Ms. Nam.

43:32.151 --> 43:34.486
Oh, I see. You're already here?

43:35.738 --> 43:36.572
Right.

43:37.823 --> 43:39.491
The room number is...

43:42.077 --> 43:43.120
Just a moment.

43:50.753 --> 43:52.171
Did you order room service?

43:58.302 --> 44:00.095
Where did he go?

44:51.522 --> 44:52.356
Thanks.

45:00.197 --> 45:02.491
Alberto, no. Don't do this to me.

45:02.574 --> 45:05.119
No, Alberto. Don't be like this.
Please, no!

45:05.828 --> 45:06.829
Don't do this to me!

45:07.121 --> 45:08.455
- Shit.
- What's wrong?

45:08.539 --> 45:09.748
- Gosh!
- What's going on?

45:09.832 --> 45:12.042
Hang on, Alberto. Gosh!

45:14.044 --> 45:15.838
Alberto!

45:18.340 --> 45:19.842
Giddy-up!

45:19.925 --> 45:22.219
Alberto! Shit. Alberto, please...

45:23.387 --> 45:24.346
Don't die.

45:27.599 --> 45:28.434
Gang-tae!

45:29.935 --> 45:31.228
I'm really okay.

45:31.854 --> 45:34.732
Sang-tae must be waiting for you,
so just take a cab home!

45:35.983 --> 45:37.776
I won't say that you ditched me!

45:38.610 --> 45:39.695
I totally understand!

45:40.112 --> 45:43.407
Because that is
what a true loyal friend would do!

45:43.907 --> 45:45.576
Shut it and just keep on pulling.

45:49.246 --> 45:53.542
ANOTHER LONG DAY, RIGHT? CHEER UP!

45:53.625 --> 45:56.503
YOU WILL MEET YOUR SOUL MATE SOON.

46:16.732 --> 46:18.233
You've changed so much.

46:18.942 --> 46:21.945
I almost couldn't recognize you
because you don't look like a hick.

46:24.239 --> 46:27.284
Has it been almost 20 years
since I moved to a different school?

46:28.702 --> 46:29.536
Yes.

46:31.538 --> 46:34.374
We just need your signature here.

46:34.875 --> 46:37.836
The doctor must've already explained
everything over the phone.

46:38.378 --> 46:40.255
You should actually do it in person--

46:40.339 --> 46:42.716
Hey, you traveled for three hours

46:42.800 --> 46:45.969
just to get my signature
on this stupid paperwork?

46:46.386 --> 46:49.431
Do you have a strong sense of duty?
Or are you a do-gooder?

46:54.353 --> 46:57.564
Our hospital is a psychiatric clinic,

46:58.232 --> 47:01.193
so we have to work with another hospital
to perform surgery.

47:01.652 --> 47:04.321
- In your father's case--
- I told you that he's dead.

47:06.448 --> 47:08.450
I'm an orphan. You know that.

47:10.869 --> 47:14.248
- But your mother is alive--
- I registered her death a long time ago.

47:15.874 --> 47:17.584
Do you know what's interesting?

47:21.922 --> 47:25.676
My dad's soul is dead,

47:26.343 --> 47:28.720
but he's physically alive like a zombie.

47:30.848 --> 47:32.099
As for my mom,

47:33.141 --> 47:35.269
she physically died many years ago.

47:37.020 --> 47:38.272
However,

47:42.025 --> 47:45.696
her soul is still alive.

47:53.954 --> 47:56.623
So between the two of them,
who's really dead?

47:58.250 --> 48:00.252
Tell me, nurse. Who's really dead?

48:02.254 --> 48:03.088
Your father...

48:04.631 --> 48:06.592
I mean, Mr. Ko Dae-hwan.

48:06.675 --> 48:09.678
He'll be in critical condition
without the surgery this time.

48:10.137 --> 48:11.346
His cognitive functions--

48:11.430 --> 48:14.016
Hey, others will think
that you're his daughter.

48:14.933 --> 48:17.519
Oh, why don't we do that?
You can be his daughter.

48:17.603 --> 48:19.021
I'll be your mom's daughter.

48:19.271 --> 48:22.941
I'll sign this consent form
if you agree to that. What do you say?

48:54.097 --> 48:55.849
Your mom is a good cook.

48:56.725 --> 48:59.937
Shall I come over for some food
like the good old days?

49:03.690 --> 49:05.651
I see that you still don't get my jokes.

49:07.903 --> 49:09.196
You're no fun.

49:12.866 --> 49:15.077
She pisses me off.

49:16.703 --> 49:18.038
She's insane.

49:18.121 --> 49:21.541
I can't believe she writes
children's book. That's bizarre.

49:21.875 --> 49:23.210
She's not "insane."

49:24.962 --> 49:26.421
She was just born that way.

49:26.505 --> 49:28.548
Gosh. Can you diagnose people at a glance

49:28.632 --> 49:31.259
now that you've worked
at mental hospitals for ten years?

49:32.094 --> 49:33.303
Stop overreacting.

49:33.387 --> 49:35.847
You fool, can you please learn
to overreact a little?

49:38.350 --> 49:40.894
You got fired and got cut
because of those lunatics.

49:40.978 --> 49:43.522
I can't believe you just left
without causing a scene.

49:43.605 --> 49:44.773
Had I done that,

49:47.025 --> 49:48.360
it would've felt nice,

49:49.778 --> 49:52.072
- but I wouldn't get my severance pay.
- Well done.

49:52.864 --> 49:56.118
Your brother got expelled from school,
and you got fired from work.

49:56.201 --> 49:57.953
You guys are two peas in a pod.

49:58.578 --> 50:00.288
It was about time I quit anyway.

50:06.294 --> 50:07.671
It's this time of the year.

50:08.672 --> 50:10.340
When the night breeze feels warm.

50:11.800 --> 50:12.634
I guess

50:15.429 --> 50:16.888
butterflies will appear soon.

50:21.184 --> 50:22.019
Right.

50:24.187 --> 50:27.357
How's Sang-tae? No signs yet?

50:29.067 --> 50:29.901
No, not yet.

50:31.069 --> 50:32.612
Then where should we go next?

50:35.615 --> 50:38.618
- Should we go to another country?
- Do you even have a passport?

50:38.702 --> 50:40.746
Sang-tae should learn English.

50:42.998 --> 50:43.832
Jae-su.

50:44.958 --> 50:46.543
Don't say anything to Sang-tae.

50:46.626 --> 50:50.380
Gosh, you only care about your brother.
I'm sick of this.

50:51.048 --> 50:52.507
I'm so jealous.

50:53.967 --> 50:54.968
You scared me.

50:57.596 --> 51:00.140
What's wrong?
Did she also hit you in the head?

51:02.642 --> 51:05.395
The autograph.
I forgot to get her autograph.

51:05.896 --> 51:08.565
- I promised him I'd get it.
- She must've hit you hard.

51:09.191 --> 51:10.025
What do I do?

51:11.109 --> 51:11.943
Oh, dear.

51:13.820 --> 51:15.822
AUTHOR KO MUN-YEONG'S AUTOGRAPH

51:26.500 --> 51:29.586
Gosh, her autograph
looks like a bunch of heroglyphs.

51:30.587 --> 51:33.256
Hieroglyphs, not "heroglyphs."

51:35.884 --> 51:37.469
Hurry up. Sang-tae is waiting.

51:46.311 --> 51:47.938
Done. Have a look.

51:49.106 --> 51:50.982
Look. It's very similar, isn't it?

51:59.157 --> 52:00.492
Nice job, Jae-su!

52:00.992 --> 52:03.120
Hey, quiet down.

52:06.081 --> 52:08.041
- Happy now?
- Yes.

52:09.167 --> 52:10.168
He'll be happy.

52:13.547 --> 52:15.549
Don't smile like that. It disgusts me.

52:17.968 --> 52:20.095
A patient said the same thing to me today.

52:21.596 --> 52:23.014
Is my smile that annoying?

52:24.224 --> 52:25.142
You don't know?

52:26.643 --> 52:27.894
You really don't know?

52:29.062 --> 52:31.314
- What?
- When you smile,

52:33.733 --> 52:35.402
you look like the Joker.

52:35.485 --> 52:38.530
With those sad eyes
and your lips pointing up like this.

52:40.448 --> 52:41.908
Look in the mirror. You'll see.

52:47.164 --> 52:47.998
Let's go.

52:56.173 --> 52:58.091
Sang-tae, I'm home.

53:05.974 --> 53:06.808
This...

53:09.769 --> 53:11.897
This is fake. It's fake.

53:11.980 --> 53:14.733
- No, it's real--
- This is fake.

53:15.066 --> 53:16.234
- That's…
- It's fake.

53:16.318 --> 53:19.029
- Sang-tae, wait.
- This is fake.

53:19.112 --> 53:22.782
- Goodness...
- This is fake.

53:22.866 --> 53:25.785
This is fake, fake, fake. It's all fake.

53:25.869 --> 53:27.871
You lied to me.

53:28.455 --> 53:31.541
- Sang-tae, I'm sorry.
- You lied to me.

53:32.751 --> 53:33.668
You lied to me?

53:33.752 --> 53:36.004
- Lying is bad.
- I was too busy today that...

53:36.087 --> 53:37.797
Lying is bad. You lied to me?

53:37.881 --> 53:40.091
Even little kids know
that it's wrong to lie.

53:40.175 --> 53:42.427
- Shall we go to the bookstore tomorrow?
- You lied?

53:42.510 --> 53:45.013
- Even a kid--
- Shall we get the dinosaur encyclopedia?

53:45.096 --> 53:47.307
- What?
- You always wanted that book.

53:49.184 --> 53:52.062
- Sang-tae?
- You lied?

53:52.771 --> 53:55.065
You lied? Why did you lie to me?

53:55.148 --> 53:59.402
- Lying is bad.
- Gosh, you poor thing.

54:01.821 --> 54:04.366
This is all Ko Mun-yeong's fault.

54:04.449 --> 54:07.369
I'm going to burn all these books!
What is this?

54:07.452 --> 54:09.412
- Why would a boy feed on nightmares?
- No!

54:09.496 --> 54:12.874
- No, don't.
- I'll burn all these books.

54:12.958 --> 54:14.542
- No!
- No? Why not?

54:14.626 --> 54:17.087
- It's mine. Don't do this.
- I'll burn them all.

54:17.170 --> 54:18.797
- Hello.
- Let go.

54:18.880 --> 54:22.175
I am Lee Sang-in,
the CEO of SangSangESang Publishers,

54:22.259 --> 54:24.636
a children's book publisher.

54:27.305 --> 54:31.476
First of all,
I'd like to sincerely apologize

54:31.559 --> 54:35.021
for the unfortunate incident
between you and our author earlier today.

54:37.440 --> 54:39.401
I'd like to speak with you

54:39.484 --> 54:41.945
if you can spare a moment
out of your busy schedule.

54:42.028 --> 54:43.905
It'd be greatly appreciated

54:43.989 --> 54:46.658
if you could stop by our office tomorrow.

54:47.701 --> 54:50.245
Please don't say no.

54:50.870 --> 54:53.707
I'd really like to meet you. Please.

55:02.757 --> 55:05.051
- Please!
- Why would you read children's books?

55:05.135 --> 55:07.721
You don't understand art.
Art is a beautiful thing.

55:07.804 --> 55:09.973
What do you mean I don't understand art?

55:10.056 --> 55:12.309
Naughty erotica books are what I call art.

55:12.392 --> 55:14.644
- This is--
- Go away. Just go home.

55:14.728 --> 55:16.855
- Just leave.
- Come on. I like you so much.

55:20.692 --> 55:23.236
Of course. I knew it. Let's see.

55:25.280 --> 55:26.114
Sure.

55:27.198 --> 55:29.909
"Sure"?
Gosh, that doesn't sound good.

55:29.993 --> 55:32.454
Around 6 p.m., at a Seoul hospital,
a man arranged

55:32.537 --> 55:35.707
- to be transferred to the police
- I have a bad feeling.

55:35.790 --> 55:38.710
after attempting to take his own life
as well as his daughter's

55:38.793 --> 55:41.796
was found dead in solitary confinement.

55:41.880 --> 55:43.923
The police are investigating his death.

55:44.382 --> 55:47.010
He caused a scene
at a book reading event

55:47.093 --> 55:49.346
which was held
for children in the hospital,

55:49.429 --> 55:53.016
but the security guards
were able to stop him immediately.

56:25.465 --> 56:28.760
He has such beautiful eyes.

56:41.106 --> 56:42.065
Do you know this?

56:42.941 --> 56:46.194
In this world,
there are people who deserve to die.

56:46.277 --> 56:50.407
But some thoughtful freaks
kill them for us in secret.

56:50.490 --> 56:53.952
That is why the clueless civilians
can sleep peacefully at night,

56:54.452 --> 56:55.954
completely unaware of it.

57:09.676 --> 57:11.845
What the…
I told you not to look down on me.

57:13.096 --> 57:14.806
Yes, I won't.

57:14.889 --> 57:17.725
- Stop him.
- Okay, go back to sleep.

57:37.412 --> 57:38.538
JAE-SU IS NOT ALLOWED!

58:03.021 --> 58:04.814
THE BOY WHO FED ON NIGHTMARES 

58:34.135 --> 58:37.847
"The boy woke up
from another awful nightmare.

58:40.934 --> 58:43.353
Bad memories from the past
that he wanted to forget

58:43.895 --> 58:46.231
were replayed in his dreams every night

58:47.607 --> 58:49.234
and haunted him nonstop.

58:53.738 --> 58:56.741
Years went by,
and the boy became an adult.

58:57.951 --> 58:59.619
He no longer had nightmares.

59:00.161 --> 59:02.830
But for some strange reason,
he wasn't happy at all.

59:05.083 --> 59:07.293
One night,
a blood moon filled the night sky,

59:07.627 --> 59:09.420
and the witch finally showed up again

59:10.129 --> 59:13.132
to take what he had promised
in return for granting his wish.

59:14.217 --> 59:16.928
And he shouted at her
with so much resentment.

59:23.351 --> 59:25.395
'All my bad memories are gone. But why…

59:26.563 --> 59:28.356
Why can't I become happy?'

59:32.277 --> 59:35.530
Then the witch took his soul
as they had promised

59:35.905 --> 59:37.156
and told him this.

59:40.785 --> 59:42.453
'Hurtful, painful memories.

59:43.830 --> 59:45.206
Memories of deep regrets.

59:47.208 --> 59:49.335
Memories of hurting others and being hurt.

59:50.753 --> 59:52.589
Memories of being abandoned.

59:53.881 --> 59:58.052
Only those with such memories
buried in their hearts

59:58.928 --> 01:00:01.556
can become stronger, more passionate,

01:00:02.432 --> 01:00:03.975
and emotionally flexible.

01:00:05.184 --> 01:00:07.937
And only those can attain happiness.'"

01:00:43.806 --> 01:00:45.099
Never forget today.

01:00:54.692 --> 01:00:55.818
You can't fall asleep?

01:00:57.528 --> 01:00:58.821
Where's my dad?

01:01:00.365 --> 01:01:02.909
Everything will be okay. Don't worry.

01:01:04.410 --> 01:01:07.205
Will the police take him?

01:01:08.998 --> 01:01:12.085
Will he be locked away
in a mental institution?

01:01:14.379 --> 01:01:17.882
Are you scared
that he'll show up again and harass you?

01:01:19.008 --> 01:01:20.551
That won't happen again.

01:01:22.512 --> 01:01:23.763
My dad...

01:01:26.057 --> 01:01:27.433
My dad is

01:01:28.643 --> 01:01:30.395
not a bad person.

01:01:31.229 --> 01:01:32.814
He's just not well.

01:01:33.481 --> 01:01:35.483
He's mentally ill.

01:01:37.652 --> 01:01:38.736
So please...

01:01:39.654 --> 01:01:42.031
Don't let the police take him.

01:01:43.199 --> 01:01:45.493
Please allow me to live with him.

01:01:47.203 --> 01:01:49.080
I want to live with my dad.

01:01:50.331 --> 01:01:52.083
I want to live with him.

01:01:53.710 --> 01:01:55.920
I miss my dad.

01:01:56.003 --> 01:01:58.423
- "So don't forget any of it.
- Dad...

01:01:58.506 --> 01:02:01.759
Remember it all and overcome it.
If you don't overcome it,

01:02:02.510 --> 01:02:07.306
you'll always be a kid
whose soul never grows."

01:03:07.492 --> 01:03:09.285
What? Butterflies...

01:03:10.703 --> 01:03:12.079
No, those butterflies!

01:03:38.689 --> 01:03:41.776
- What? What's going on?
- Butterflies!

01:03:41.859 --> 01:03:43.736
- What's the matter?
- Butterflies...

01:03:43.820 --> 01:03:45.530
- Sang-tae.
- Butterflies...

01:03:45.613 --> 01:03:47.615
Gosh, those butterflies...

01:03:47.698 --> 01:03:49.784
Butterflies! Those butterflies!

01:03:50.409 --> 01:03:53.746
- Don't! I'm sorry!
- They're back. Those damn butterflies.

01:03:54.205 --> 01:03:55.957
Those butterflies!

01:03:56.040 --> 01:03:59.752
They said they'll kill me.
The butterflies will kill me!

01:03:59.836 --> 01:04:02.713
They're coming to kill me!

01:04:02.797 --> 01:04:05.341
- I have to run away.
- Sang-tae.

01:04:05.424 --> 01:04:08.010
I have to go. I must run away!

01:04:08.928 --> 01:04:10.179
Go away!

01:04:17.395 --> 01:04:18.604
Hey, Gang-tae!

01:04:18.688 --> 01:04:21.315
It's not even the peak moving season.
Why move out?

01:04:21.399 --> 01:04:23.025
Gosh, I can't believe this.

01:04:24.026 --> 01:04:24.861
Gang-tae!

01:04:26.237 --> 01:04:28.948
You still have months left on your lease.
Why do you...

01:04:29.031 --> 01:04:30.616
Gosh, you scared me.

01:04:30.700 --> 01:04:32.451
Mister, you slept here again?

01:04:32.535 --> 01:04:34.787
Then you need to chip in
for the water usage!

01:04:35.663 --> 01:04:37.248
Go bring the young man.

01:04:37.331 --> 01:04:40.251
We're friends. Why is he a young man
when you call me a mister?

01:04:40.334 --> 01:04:42.670
Cut it out. Where is he?

01:04:43.087 --> 01:04:44.463
I wonder too.

01:04:44.797 --> 01:04:47.341
Where on earth did he go so early?

01:05:07.612 --> 01:05:08.863
Mr. Moon Gang-tae?

01:05:12.283 --> 01:05:13.492
Hello.

01:05:13.993 --> 01:05:16.621
My boss is on his way back
from the print shop now.

01:05:16.704 --> 01:05:18.706
He said he'll be about ten minutes late.

01:05:47.109 --> 01:05:48.069
This way.

01:05:49.862 --> 01:05:52.114
Please wait here for a moment.

01:05:52.615 --> 01:05:53.449
Sure.

01:06:02.708 --> 01:06:06.504
THE HAND, THE MONKFISH

01:06:15.179 --> 01:06:16.681
AUTHOR KO MUN-YEONG

01:06:37.994 --> 01:06:41.038
Guys, she's here!
Clear your desks. Tidy up.

01:06:43.916 --> 01:06:44.917
Hurry.

01:06:56.345 --> 01:06:57.763
Who sits here?

01:06:59.181 --> 01:07:01.142
The accounting manager. Why do you ask?

01:07:02.309 --> 01:07:03.394
This is pretty.

01:07:03.477 --> 01:07:05.229
- I want it--
- Then you can have it.

01:07:05.855 --> 01:07:07.189
I was going to anyway.

01:07:14.238 --> 01:07:17.491
- Ms. Ko, what brings you by?
- Zombie Kid is coming out today.

01:07:17.575 --> 01:07:19.493
- Where's Mr. Lee?
- Well...

01:08:02.578 --> 01:08:03.412
What a sight.

01:08:13.047 --> 01:08:14.715
You look dashing in regular clothes.

01:08:15.508 --> 01:08:18.260
Like an escort who's here to harass me
to pay off my tab.

01:08:21.138 --> 01:08:24.225
I thought you'd be different,
but I was obviously wrong.

01:08:24.809 --> 01:08:25.935
How much did he offer?

01:08:26.352 --> 01:08:29.146
If you can't talk politely,
at least try not to be so cryptic.

01:08:29.230 --> 01:08:31.440
And look at you talking to me so casually.

01:08:32.817 --> 01:08:34.151
I practically stabbed you.

01:08:37.446 --> 01:08:39.782
- What about it?
- How much did Mr. Lee offer you

01:08:40.950 --> 01:08:42.201
to compensate you for that

01:08:42.535 --> 01:08:45.579
as well as to make sure
you won't tell anyone about it?

01:08:49.041 --> 01:08:50.668
I guess this has always worked.

01:08:50.751 --> 01:08:52.336
Verbal consolation is useless.

01:08:52.419 --> 01:08:53.504
Money is the best.

01:08:55.381 --> 01:08:56.382
Not to me.

01:08:57.216 --> 01:08:59.218
Then what do you want? Sex?

01:09:00.553 --> 01:09:01.971
Is it worth more than money?

01:09:05.391 --> 01:09:06.600
Then why are you here?

01:09:06.684 --> 01:09:09.812
If not for money or sex,
what are you here for?

01:09:14.608 --> 01:09:15.568
I was hoping

01:09:19.780 --> 01:09:21.115
I could see you

01:09:22.575 --> 01:09:23.409
again.

01:09:27.371 --> 01:09:28.205
Your eyes.

01:09:30.249 --> 01:09:31.876
I wanted to see them again.

01:09:35.754 --> 01:09:36.589
My eyes?

01:09:38.132 --> 01:09:38.966
Your eyes

01:09:41.927 --> 01:09:44.054
remind me of someone I used to know.

01:09:48.058 --> 01:09:49.059
Who is that person?

01:09:51.854 --> 01:09:53.355
Someone who's messed up

01:09:56.942 --> 01:09:58.944
and has no conscience.

01:09:59.987 --> 01:10:00.988
A woman

01:10:02.948 --> 01:10:04.200
whose eyes

01:10:06.118 --> 01:10:07.203
utterly lacked warmth.

01:10:14.668 --> 01:10:15.544
That woman...

01:10:20.216 --> 01:10:21.342
Were you afraid of her?

01:10:26.222 --> 01:10:27.097
No, the opposite.

01:10:45.074 --> 01:10:47.826
I liked her.

01:12:00.441 --> 01:12:01.650
Are you that excited?

01:12:01.734 --> 01:12:04.903
"Dear Sang-tae!
Please come to my book launch party."

01:12:04.987 --> 01:12:07.614
It's boring to say
that we're destined for each other.

01:12:07.698 --> 01:12:09.074
I thought I was on the run…

01:12:09.700 --> 01:12:10.701
Don't touch my hair!

01:12:10.784 --> 01:12:12.202
because of my brother.

01:12:13.078 --> 01:12:14.288
Coward.

01:12:14.371 --> 01:12:16.582
Where is Ko Mun-yeong?

01:12:16.999 --> 01:12:19.585
You won't end up well
if you get involved with her.

01:12:20.878 --> 01:12:23.297
- Don't go.
- I want you to be my safety pin.

01:12:23.630 --> 01:12:27.217
Keep me under control
so that I won't explode.

01:12:36.268 --> 01:12:40.814
The boy woke up
from another awful nightmare.

01:12:41.607 --> 01:12:44.485
Bad memories from the past
that he wanted to forget

01:12:44.568 --> 01:12:47.863
were replayed in his dreams every night

01:12:47.946 --> 01:12:50.574
and haunted him nonstop.

01:12:51.325 --> 01:12:53.869
The boy was terrified of falling asleep.

01:12:53.952 --> 01:12:57.039
So one day,
he went to the witch and begged.

01:12:57.998 --> 01:13:01.001
"Please get rid of all my bad memories

01:13:01.335 --> 01:13:04.213
so that I won't ever have
a nightmare again.

01:13:05.255 --> 01:13:08.008
Then I will do everything you ask."

01:13:09.635 --> 01:13:12.262
Years went by,
and the boy became an adult.

01:13:12.596 --> 01:13:14.848
He no longer had nightmares.

01:13:15.432 --> 01:13:19.228
But for some strange reason,
he wasn't happy at all.

01:13:21.063 --> 01:13:23.399
One night,
a blood moon filled the night sky,

01:13:23.482 --> 01:13:25.317
and the witch finally showed up again

01:13:25.401 --> 01:13:28.821
to take what he had promised
in return for granting his wish.

01:13:29.154 --> 01:13:32.282
And he shouted at her
with so much resentment.

01:13:33.117 --> 01:13:35.911
"All my bad memories are gone. But why...

01:13:36.787 --> 01:13:38.705
Why can't I become happy?"

01:13:39.540 --> 01:13:43.085
Then the witch took his soul,
as they had promised,

01:13:43.168 --> 01:13:44.586
and told him this.

01:13:45.129 --> 01:13:47.172
"Hurtful, painful memories.

01:13:47.673 --> 01:13:49.466
Memories of deep regrets.

01:13:50.092 --> 01:13:53.137
Memories of hurting others and being hurt.

01:13:53.762 --> 01:13:55.639
Memories of being abandoned.

01:13:56.223 --> 01:14:00.185
Only those with such memories
buried in their hearts

01:14:00.269 --> 01:14:02.813
can become stronger, more passionate,

01:14:03.355 --> 01:14:06.066
and emotionally flexible.

01:14:06.942 --> 01:14:10.362
And only those can attain happiness.

01:14:11.196 --> 01:14:14.700
So don't forget any of it.
Remember it all and overcome it.

01:14:15.159 --> 01:14:16.535
If you don't overcome it,

01:14:17.661 --> 01:14:21.373
you'll always be a kid
whose soul never grows."

01:14:24.001 --> 01:14:25.961
Subtitle translation by Liya Choi
